{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789302639,"nonce":"JMMgshxXrjswxTG2+GD4ERGI5Go=","title":"A top-tier compile in flight outlives the heap when a VM drops","message":"VM drops its fields in declaration order: gc before engine. The engine's promoter joins its worker only in the engine's Drop, so a compile still lowering reads classes (num_fields, field_kinds_ptr) from a heap already released. Seen as SIGSEGV in wlift-promoter under the parallel e2e binary once constructor inlining read the class object during lowering; note_field_invariant had the same exposure. Fix: VM::drop stops the promoter before its fields go.","files":null}]}